<title>PAKISTAN: China said willing to provide N-plant to Pakistan.</title>
<headline>China said willing to provide N-plant to Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan said on Thursday that China was willing in principle to provide Islamabad with a second nuclear power plant, but financing was not in place.</p>
<p>China is already building a 300-megawatt nuclear power plant at Chashma in the central province of Punjab under the safeguards of the International Atomic Energy Agency.</p>
<p>Asked if China and Pakistan had discussed the feasibility of building a &quot;Chashma-2&quot; during Chinese President Jiang Zemin's visit to Islamabad this week, a Foreign Ministry spokesman said: &quot;In principle, the Chinese are willing to do so. The question of financing is yet to be resolved.&quot;</p>
<p>He did not elaborate.</p>
</text>
